IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 21A, 21B and 21C -- layer 1: failing to disclose in the regulated sector,
-- the disclosures that are protected, and what a constable must do with a disclosure.
-- "A business in the regulated sector" and "supervisory authority" are Schedule 3A, which is not among the sources: facts the
-- caller states.  Each subsection answers on its own (E1 option C); where a function gathers a subsection with its exception
-- by hand (E1 option B as guidance), its name says so: "s 21A(1) and (5)", "s 21A(8) and (9)".

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Offences (continued): the regulated sector`

§§ `s 21A Failure to disclose: regulated sector`

-- src:143 | (2) The first condition is that he—
-- src:144 | (a) knows or suspects, or
-- src:145 | (b) has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting,
-- src:146 | that another person has committed or attempted to commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18.
@ref s 21A(2) (src:143-146)
