-- src:142 | (1) A person commits an offence if each of the following three conditions is satisfied.
-- src:143 | (2) The first condition is that he—
-- src:144 | (a) knows or suspects, or
-- src:145 | (b) has reasonable grounds for knowing or suspecting,
-- src:146 | that another person has committed or attempted to commit an offence under any of sections 15 to 18.
-- src:147 | (3) The second condition is that the information or other matter—
-- src:148 | (a) on which his knowledge or suspicion is based, or
-- src:149 | (b) which gives reasonable grounds for such knowledge or suspicion,
-- src:150 | came to him in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
-- src:151 | (4) The third condition is that he does not disclose the information or other matter to a constable or a nominated officer as soon as is practicable after it comes to him.
-- src:152 | (5) But a person does not commit an offence under this section if—
-- src:153 | (a) he has a reasonable excuse for not disclosing the information or other matter;
-- src:154 | (b) he is a professional legal adviser or relevant professional adviser and the information or other matter came to him in privileged circumstances ; or
-- src:155 | (c) subsection (5A) applies to him.
-- src:156 | (5A) This subsection applies to a person if—
-- src:157 | (a) the person is employed by, or is in partnership with, a professional legal adviser or relevant professional adviser to provide the adviser with assistance or support,
-- src:158 | (b) the information or other matter comes to the person in connection with the provision of such assistance or support, and
-- src:159 | (c) the information or other matter came to the adviser in privileged circumstances.
@ref s 21A(1) and (5) (src:142-155) (src:156-159)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Regulated sector facts`
      `the exceptions` IS A `Exception facts`
      `the assistance` IS A `Assistance facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21A(1) and (5) the person commits an offence under section 21A` IS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But a person does not commit an offence under this section if—"
        IF `s 21A(5) the person does not commit an offence under section 21A` `the exceptions` `the assistance` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE `s 21A(1) the person commits an offence if each of the three conditions is satisfied` `the facts`

-- src:160 | (6) In deciding whether a person committed an offence under this section the court must consider whether he followed any relevant guidance which was at the time concerned—
-- src:161 | (a) issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body,
-- src:162 | (b) approved by the Treasury, and
-- src:163 | (c) published in a manner it approved as appropriate in its opinion to bring the guidance to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it.
@ref s 21A(6) (src:160-163)
GIVEN `the guidance` IS A `Guidance facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21A(6) the guidance is relevant guidance the court must consider` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the guidance`'s `relevant guidance which was at the time concerned`
           AND `the guidance`'s `issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body`
           AND `the guidance`'s `approved by the Treasury`
           AND `the guidance`'s `published in a manner the Treasury approved as appropriate to bring it to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court must consider whether he followed any relevant guidance which was at the time concerned— (a) issued ... (b) approved ... (c) published" (guidance outside (a) to (c) is not said to be irrelevant)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:160 | (6) In deciding whether a person committed an offence under this section the court must consider whether he followed any relevant guidance which was at the time concerned—
-- src:161 | (a) issued by a supervisory authority or any other appropriate body,
-- src:162 | (b) approved by the Treasury, and
-- src:163 | (c) published in a manner it approved as appropriate in its opinion to bring the guidance to the attention of persons likely to be affected by it.
@ref s 21A(6) (src:160-163)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 21A(6) the court must consider whether the person followed the relevant guidance` IS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `consider whether the person followed the relevant guidance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "s 21A(6): the court did not consider whether the person followed relevant guidance issued, approved and published as the subsection requires"

