-- src:178 | (12) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:179 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years or to a fine or to both;
-- src:180 | (b) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both.
@ref s 21A(12) (src:178-180)
GIVEN `the route of conviction` IS A `Conviction route`
      `the statutory maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
DECIDE `s 21A(12) the ceiling of the penalty for an offence under s 21A` IS
    CONSIDER `the route of conviction`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF (5 TIMES 12), `No ceiling is stated`
                                            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "or to a fine or to both" states no ceiling for the fine
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF 6, `A fine not exceeding` `the statutory maximum`

