§§ `s 21C Disclosures to the National Crime Agency`

-- src:200 | (1) Where a disclosure is made under a provision of this Part to a constable, the constable must disclose it in full as soon as practicable after it has been made to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of that provision by the Director General of that Agency.
@ref s 21C(1) (src:200)
GIVEN `a disclosure is made under a provision of this Part to a constable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21C(1) the constable must pass the disclosure in full to an authorised National Crime Agency officer` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a disclosure is made under a provision of this Part to a constable`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a disclosure is made under a provision of this Part to a constable"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:200 | (1) Where a disclosure is made under a provision of this Part to a constable, the constable must disclose it in full as soon as practicable after it has been made to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of that provision by the Director General of that Agency.
@ref s 21C(1) (src:200)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part III` `Act under Part III`
DECIDE `s 21C(1) the constable must disclose it in full to an authorised National Crime Agency officer` IS
    PARTY `a constable`
    MUST `disclose the disclosure in full to an authorised National Crime Agency officer`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a constable` BECAUSE "s 21C(1): the constable did not disclose the disclosure in full, as soon as practicable, to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of that provision"

